1
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Re-Animated is a comedy, family, animation film directed by Bruce Hurwit.

2
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Jimmy is the kid everybody ignores and uses.

3
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:48,000
One day, he gets into a freak accident.

4
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:42,000
The only way for him to survive is a brain transplant.

5
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:36,000
He gets the brain of Milt Appleday, a famous cartoon creator.

6
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:30,000
And when he wakes up, he can see cartoons!

7
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:24,000
Jimmy Roberts, played by Dominic Janes.

8
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:18,000
Jimmy's Dad, played by Bil Dwyer.

9
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:12,000
Captain Roberts, played by Rachel Quaintance.

10
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Nurse, played by Jennifer De Minco.

11
00:42:54,000 --> 00:43:00,000
Head of Appleday Board, played by Neil Flynn.

12
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:54,000
Scott / Dancer, played by Tucker Barkley.

13
00:50:42,000 --> 00:50:48,000
Re-Animated is a 2006 American live-action animated teen fantasy-comedy
television film that aired on Cartoon Network on December 8, 2006.

14
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:42,000
It was the first original production on the genre for the network.

15
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
It was released on DVD on September 11, 2007, and serves as a pilot for the follow-up
series Out of Jimmy's Head, which premiered on September 14, 2007.

16
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
It received negative reviews from critics upon release.

17
01:06:18,000 --> 01:06:24,000
The film's animation was produced by Renegade Animation, which
previously produced Hi Hi Puffy AmiYumi for Cartoon Network.

18
01:10:12,000 --> 01:10:18,000
The film explores themes of alien, theme park, brain transplant.

19
01:14:06,000 --> 01:14:12,000
The tone is lighthearted.
